NAME
       tty - print the name of the terminal on standard input

SYNOPSIS
       tty [-s]

DESCRIPTION
       tty prints the device of the terminal connected to standard input,
       for example /dev/tty2 on a text console. Terminal windows of the
       graphical session report /dev/pts.

OPTIONS
       -s, --silent
           print nothing, only set the exit status

EXIT STATUS
       0 when standard input is a terminal, 1 otherwise.

SEE ALSO
       chvt(1)
